 6 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 2f8ec46..45db6ee 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -43,13 +43,13 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **Overlays.** One `a.dlg` (`dialog` with a `dialogKind`) drives every modal through `a.dialogs`. The file preview is a separate overlay (`a.pv`, `previewOverlay`). The image preview and the grid/list thumbnails share `ui.ElementTransition{Match: thumbMatch{fsid}}`. The source thumbnail is skipped while `a.previewing(f)`, so the image grows out of it and shrinks back.
 
-**File clipboard and shortcuts.** The browser's keys are handled in `app/ops.go`'s `fileActions` once per `filesPage` frame, yielding while a dialog, the preview, a rename or a folder being named is open. Cmd-C/X put the chosen files in `a.fileClip` (`app/fileclip.go`), an in-memory `fileClipboard{files, from, cut, cutSet, gen}` — never the system clipboard, as a netdisk path means nothing elsewhere. A cut fills `cutSet` by path, so a row's `isCut` says in constant time whether it shows the `待移动` chip; `putFiles` bumps `App.fileClipGen`, and sign-out clears the clipboard. Cmd-V pastes that clipboard through the picker's `place`/`moveOrCopyAfter`, which asks about names a folder has exactly as `复制到…` does; only when the file clipboard is empty does it fall back to `openClipboardShare`, the share-link behavior it had before, while Cmd-Shift-V always opens a share link. Pasting runs on goroutines through `a.run`, and the `after` callback runs only when the netdisk operation succeeded: a cut then clears the clipboard only if `fileClip.gen` is still the one it pasted, so a cut made while the first is moving survives. Cmd-Shift-C copies paths to the system clipboard, Cmd-A selects every non-temporary row in both views, and F5 refreshes as Cmd-R does.
+**File clipboard and shortcuts.** The browser's keys are handled in `app/ops.go`'s `fileActions` once per `filesPage` frame, yielding while a dialog, the preview, a rename or a folder being named is open. Cmd-C/X put the chosen files in `a.fileClip` (`app/fileclip.go`), an in-memory `fileClipboard{files, from, cut, cutSet, gen}` — never the system clipboard, as a netdisk path means nothing elsewhere. A cut fills `cutSet` by path, so a row's `isCut` says in constant time whether it shows the `待移动` chip; `putFiles` bumps `App.fileClipGen`, and sign-out clears the clipboard. Cmd-V pastes that clipboard through the picker's `place`/`moveOrCopyAfter`, which asks about names a folder has exactly as `复制到…` does; only when the file clipboard is empty does it fall back to `openClipboardShare`, the share-link behavior it had before, while Cmd-Shift-V always opens a share link. Pasting runs on goroutines through `a.run`, and the `after` callback runs only when the netdisk operation succeeded: a cut then clears the clipboard only if `fileClip.gen` is still the one it pasted, so a cut made while the first is moving survives. Cmd-Shift-C copies paths to the system clipboard, Cmd-A selects every non-temporary row in both views, and F5 refreshes as Cmd-R does. A held key acts once: auto-repeats of these file keys are ignored, and while an operation is busy the browser takes no file key, so a paste cannot start twice.
 
 **Netdisk client (`internal/baidu`).** `baidu.Open(creds)` builds a `baidupcs.BaiduPCS` from cookies and never touches BaiduPCS-Go's global config. It also turns TLS verification back on (the library disables it). Two code paths:
 - **Library calls** for `LocateDownload` (download links, which need the uid, fetched once from Tieba) and upload (`internal/pcsport`, ported from BaiduPCS-Go's `internal/` under Apache-2.0).
 - **The pan.baidu.com web API**, called directly through `getJSON`/`postForm` against `c.base`, for everything else: list (with `web=1` for thumbnails), file manager ops, recycle bin, shares, `cloud_dl`. Writes carry a `bdstoken`, fetched from `/api/loginStatus`.
 
-**Someone else's share links** (`OpenShare`/`SharedDir`/`SaveShared` in `internal/baidu/share.go`): `/share/verify` trades the password for a `randsk`, which every later call carries as `sekey` and in the `BDCLND` cookie. An old `BDCLND` for `.baidu.com`, imported with the cookies, is sent first and hides the new one, so `OpenShare` overwrites it. `/api/shorturlinfo` gives the share's dates, `/share/list` its entries (numbers as strings at the top, as numbers in folders), the share's page the sharer's name and photo, and `/share/transfer` saves chosen fs_ids. The app (`app/sharelink.go`) opens a share link from the clipboard only when the user asks for it, with the folder toolbar's link button or Cmd-V in the browser; the view never reads the clipboard by itself, as its owner can make GTK's synchronous read wait and freeze the main thread. fakepan knows `fakepan.DemoShare` and the account's own shares.
+**Someone else's share links** (`OpenShare`/`SharedDir`/`SaveShared` in `internal/baidu/share.go`): `/share/verify` trades the password for a `randsk`, which every later call carries as `sekey` and in the `BDCLND` cookie. An old `BDCLND` for `.baidu.com`, imported with the cookies, is sent first and hides the new one, so `OpenShare` overwrites it. `/api/shorturlinfo` gives the share's dates, `/share/list` its entries (numbers as strings at the top, as numbers in folders), the share's page the sharer's name and photo, and `/share/transfer` saves chosen fs_ids. The app (`app/sharelink.go`) opens a share link from the clipboard only when the user asks for it, with the folder toolbar's link button, Cmd-Shift-V, or Cmd-V while no files are cut or copied; the view never reads the clipboard by itself, as its owner can make GTK's synchronous read wait and freeze the main thread. fakepan knows `fakepan.DemoShare` and the account's own shares.
 
 `baidu.OpenAt(creds, base)` points the client at a fake server. `c.fake()` swaps in fake-friendly behavior in the few library-bound paths (download URL, upload). Errno -6/-4/111 maps to `ErrNotLoggedIn`, which signs the user out.
 
